Android's headers can define PTHREAD_ONCE_INIT without declaring pthread_once.
Include pthread.h explicitly for the thread-safe CRC64 table initialization.

--- a/libdispatch/dcrc64.c
+++ b/libdispatch/dcrc64.c
@@ -48,9 +48,7 @@
    pthread library for table initialization.  In that case, the initialization
    will not be thread-safe.  That's fine, so long as it can be assured that
    there is only one thread using crc64(). */
-#if 0
 #include <pthread.h>            /* link with -lpthread */
-#endif
 
